# Git before deploy

When the user **approves** commit/push/deploy (see `ask-commit-push-deploy.mdc`):

1. Stage relevant project changes (never secrets: `.env`, keys, pem, hardcoded passwords).
2. Create a clear, detailed commit message (why + what).
3. `git push` to GitHub (`origin` → `Avazov03/Admin-Zonic`).
4. Only then deploy to the server.

Do not deploy-only and leave git behind. If push fails, fix auth/remote before deploying.

Default behavior: **ask first** — do not auto-run unless the user said to.
